cmp — Compare two inputs byte by byte
cmp [OPTION]… FILE1 [FILE2 [SKIP1 [SKIP2]]]

-b, --print-bytes     Show the values and representations of differing bytes.
-c, --print-chars     Historical alias for -b.
-i, --ignore-initial=N[:M]   Skip N bytes on the left and M on the right (default N).
-l, --verbose         List decimal positions and octal values.
-n, --bytes=N         Compare at most N bytes.
-s, --quiet, --silent Report comparison status only.
-v, --version         Show the component version.
    --help            Show this help.
    --                End option processing.

A dash or an omitted second file selects standard input. Positions begin at 1 after skipping. Counts accept decimal, octal (0), hexadecimal (0x) and suffixes K through Y, kB, MiB and their multiples. -l and -s are incompatible.

cmp -bl a.bin b.bin
cat a.bin | cmp -s b.bin -

Status: 0 equal, 1 different, 2 trouble.
Capabilities: read each delegated file and selected input stream. Comparison reads in blocks. Help and version use only the output stream.
